# ── PROPRIETARY / CLOSED SOURCE ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The following are NOT part of the open source CLI.
# They live in private repositories.

# docs/ is public (user + contributor docs). Operational runbooks, launch copy,
# billing and compliance notes stay local in docs/internal/ — back them up in a
# private repo, not here.
docs/internal/

# Production deploy script — it targets tunr's own server (host, paths, SSH).
# Self-hosters follow docs/SELF_HOSTING.md instead.
update.sh

# Relay server binary (build artefact)
relay/server

# Freemium / internal — keep locally, do not publish
.tunr.schema.json
CODEOWNERS

# Dashboard + landing page (proprietary — not published to GitHub)
landing/

# ── SECRETS / CREDENTIALS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEVER commit these. Ever.
supabase.json
paddle.json
.env
.env.*
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.secret

# Node.js (for SDK and dashboard)
node_modules/
.next/
.vercel/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Pivot planning material — reference only, not part of the module.
# (ref/tunrpivot/*.go are stray copies whose package names collide, which
#  breaks `go build ./...` and `go test ./...` — the release gate.)
ref/

# Stray relay binary built with `go build -o relay-server`
relay/relay-server
